Bundled Git for Windows (MinGit) — GNU GPL v2 (separately licensed)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Binary distributions of Lares for Windows bundle a copy of Git for Windows in
its minimal "MinGit" form (hereafter "the Program"), used as a fallback Git
runtime when no compatible Git is already installed. The Program is NOT part of
Lares' own Apache-2.0-licensed code: it is a separate program, licensed under
the GNU General Public License, version 2.

  - Full license text:  third_party/git-for-windows/GPLv2.txt
  - Pinned version:     third_party/git-for-windows/mingit-manifest.json
  - Written source offer (GPLv2 §3(b), 3-year):
                        third_party/git-for-windows/SOURCE-OFFER.txt
  - Upstream source URL template:
                        third_party/git-for-windows/SOURCE-URL.txt

Corresponding source availability: the exact corresponding source code for the
pinned version of the Program is retained by Edward Turk and is available on
request for at least three years, as stated in the written offer above. The
canonical upstream source is the git-for-windows/git repository on GitHub.

Git config note: Lares never writes the user's global (~/.gitconfig) or system
Git configuration. The bundled Program carries its own inert system config at
mingit/etc/gitconfig containing only `[core] longpaths = true`; that config
applies solely to the bundled Program and is not consulted when Lares' internal
resolution or the user's shell uses a system-installed Git. Lares reads the
user's own Git configuration normally but never mutates global, system, or repo
Git trust or configuration.
